            <ArticleTitle>Pin hole balloon rupture during coronary angioplasty causing dissection and occlusion of the coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case with pinhole rupture of the balloon of a Probe (USCI) coronary angioplasty catheter with resultant dissection and occlusion of the coronary artery is presented. The possible mechanism, predictors and precautions to prevent this complication are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
